---
import ContentPage from '../../../layouts/ContentPage.astro';
import gebiedenData from '../../../data/gebieden.json';

const locale = 'en' as const;
const voorbeelden = ['cuijk', 'boxmeer', 'arnhem', 'oss'];
const gebieden = gebiedenData.gebieden.filter((g: any) => voorbeelden.includes(g.slug));
---

<ContentPage
  title="Vierdaagse Logeren for international participants"
  description="Practical information for foreign walkers and visitors: language, booking systems, travel distance and planning around the Four Days Marches."
  locale={locale}
  h1="For international participants"
>
  <p>
    47,000 walkers from 77 countries take part in the Vierdaagse. If you're coming from outside the
    Netherlands, a few practical things work slightly differently than for a Dutch participant.
  </p>

  <h2>Language and booking systems</h2>
  <p>
    Large platforms like Booking.com operate in English, but private hosts in the region don't always
    communicate in English. Expect Dutch-language replies to a direct enquiry with a local host — a
    short, friendly question in English is generally understood fine, even if the reply comes back in Dutch.
  </p>

  <h2>Travel distance: a real option, not a last resort</h2>
  <p>
    For a Dutch participant arriving by car, "half an hour further" is a minor inconvenience. For an
    international visitor travelling by train or plane, that trade-off looks different. Still, staying
    a bit further from Nijmegen is often a deliberate, cost-effective choice — not just a fallback
    when the city itself is full.
  </p>

  <table class="gebied-tabel">
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Place</th><th>Distance</th><th>Public transport</th><th>Station</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {gebieden.map((g: any) => (
        <tr>
          <td><a href={`/en/gebied/${g.slug}`}>{g.naam}</a></td>
          <td>{g.afstandKm}</td>
          <td>{g.ov}</td>
          <td>{g.station}</td>
        </tr>
      ))}
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <p>
    All of these are reachable by train, with travel times between 12 and 20 minutes to Nijmegen.
    See the full overview of <a href="/en/gebied">all areas around Nijmegen</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Planning your arrival and departure</h2>
  <p>
    Nijmegen's city centre is considerably busier than usual during Vierdaagse week, especially around
    midday and early evening. Allow extra travel time to and from your accommodation on walking days,
    and check the current NS timetable for last trains — this can differ from a regular week during the event.
  </p>
  <p class="callout callout--open">
    Check the current timetable and any shuttle services close to the event date itself; this varies per edition.
  </p>
</ContentPage>

<style>
  .gebied-tabel { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin: var(--space-4) 0; }
  .gebied-tabel th, .gebied-tabel td {
    text-align: left;
    padding: var(--space-2) var(--space-3);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }
  .gebied-tabel th { color: var(--color-primary); font-weight: 600; }
</style>
